[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
arcana-agent runs on each host, as root; see arcana-agent(8).  The short
way is to enrol the host from the console, which gives a one-time command:

  arcana-enrol -s https://console.example <token>

The console (CONSOLE option), arcana-console(8), serves as an
unprivileged user:

  pw useradd arcana -d /var/db/arcana -s /usr/sbin/nologin
  install -d -o arcana -m 0700 /var/db/arcana
  edit %%PREFIX%%/etc/arcana/web.conf (its server { } and the rest)
  sysrc arcana_console_enable=YES && service arcana_console start

The host the console runs on is its first: start its agent, and the
console adds it by itself, over the agent's local socket, which the
group arcana may use:

  sysrc arcana_agent_enable=YES && service arcana_agent start

Its TLS certificate may be RSA or EC.  The first login needs the token in /var/db/arcana/setup-token.
EOM
}
]
